{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 5784e23d8197d5cbea819849af3830131449c874, tree 87563b4cd368e1ae3b5dd7028d3f8a428d28b81a, on builder/gs4-p1-on-ls3-20261115, all 25 artifacts, for request a53a9d08 under my promise 9a583316 and standing da772676. This verdict names all three implementations: GS-4 (request 349bdc90, promise f7f7040b, report e9c95bae, the GS-4 note, primary), P1 (request bea87570, promise 3acac812, report 854a4957, the P1 note) and LS-4 (request 8ba43279, promise 76c1102d, report 9dd914cd, `scripts/test-celld-proxy.mjs`). `gs review --prepare` resolved all three bindings and reports at this head, with each request closing on the sealed receipt. The approved LS-3 head 7bb7060a is an ancestor. This verdict covers the 25 paths from 7bb7060a to this head. The landing order stays CE-2 and LW-1, then LS-3, then this head.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- GS-4. `scripts/pins.mjs` runs compatibility, then six existing whole owners: Security, release reproduction, Page assets, Card resources, CLI examples and MCP inventory. Each owner runs as a child with `MCP_WRITE_DOCS` removed, so the inventory owner can only compare. The first failure or signal stops later owners. After each owner and at the end, the script reports a total above 60 seconds as a failure. No timer kills an owner. `scripts/gate.sh` runs `pins` before `npm test` on a full selection only, and a notes-only head still skips both. `package.json` adds only the `pins` script. `docs/testing.md` replaces four separate pre-gate rules with one: run `npm run pins` at the exact head, and require exit 0 within 60 seconds.\n- LS-4. `backendTail` now takes the run's secrets. It decodes UTF-8 with a streaming decoder and replaces each exact secret with one fixed marker. It does this before the 12-line, 512-byte clipping. It tries the longest secret first. While the unread text could still be the start of a longer secret, it holds that text back. Between chunks it keeps only that possible prefix and any incomplete UTF-8 bytes. `snapshot` previews the held text without changing that state. The secrets are the `SESSION_SECRET` text and the operator key in base64url, base64 and hex. The script reads the planned operator key before the backend starts and refuses to start without it. It adds the key again after the smoke and clears both key buffers in `finally`.\n- P1, the definition. `examples/lending/publisher/definition.ts` is a separate definition. It keeps the shipped circulation acts without their destination sends. It adds a library with an optional `publisher` party, `bind-repository` and `appoint-publisher` under `lending.staff`, `adopt-head` under staff, and `published`. `published` needs `lending.publish`, which only the agent role gains. It also needs the signer to be the appointed `publisher`, a `through` fact in this scope, and a `base` equal to the recorded head. The shipped Lending definition, pin and release do not change.\n- P1, the publisher. `publisher.ts` reads one complete summary and checks the scope, the pin, the genesis entry, a single open library, the appointment and the bound repository. It first settles or resends a kept unresolved report from custody, without signing it again. Then it reads one fixed journal cut from the cursor to the summary head, with whole coverage, no gap and a matching head hash. `fold.ts` checks each row's hash, genesis and `prev` link. It writes only `shelf/*.md` paths that pass the Git path grammar. It records each skipped write with its reason, inside the Git tree and file bounds. It builds one deterministic commit whose trailer names the scope, the genesis, the `through` fact and the base. `git.ts` uses only a canonical local bare repository and a separate work directory, through the library's closed Git environment. It writes the objects, checks that each written ID matches, and updates the branch only from the expected base. When the branch already moved, the publisher rebuilds that commit with the shared fold and requires the same bytes before it reports. The report key is the commit and library revision, so an `unsent` ending stops as `report-unsent` until the revision moves. A folded record stops as `custody-mismatch`. That follows ruling c8572723.\n- P1, the CLI. `publish.ts` reads an existing member home and its stored key. It opens a session and reads no Git credential. The owner's own Git carries the branch to a remote.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. The 25 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 7bb7060a 5784e23d`. From the gated head 50e16a76 to this head only three Markdown files change.\n- Gate, END 7471c330. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-15-gs4-p1-ls4-full-gate-attempt1/gate.log` has SHA-256 cb4205c5…, `result.json` has c6314cad…, and `final-source-correspondence.json` has 850476de…, as the request states. The log names head 50e16a76 and tree c47b82f4 with 0 changed files. The new `pins` stage passed in 16.6 seconds inside the gate. Kernel, Node 205, Counting 56, Plain 4890 with 1 skipped and Native 1158 with 2 skipped passed, and its last line is \"gate passed\". Scale selected `all` because `scripts/gate.sh` and `package.json` changed, and its cases ran inside Native. `result.json` records verification exit 0 and `PASS`. The `controls` directory holds `gs4-stale-id`, `ls4-known-secret`, `p1-current-invocation`, `p1-current-unsent` and `p1-directory-history`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 9 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. GS-4 moves the existing pinned-value owners into one early stage and changes none of them. LS-4 does the replacement inside the existing tail, before the existing limits, so every display path sees the same text. P1 keeps the publisher out of the shipped Lending definition. It reads and folds the journal in one module and reproduces commits with that same fold, so the publisher and the clone check cannot disagree on bytes.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding.\n\n- GS-4 removes `MCP_WRITE_DOCS` from the stage, so the gate cannot rewrite a document that it compares.\n- LS-4 replaces the exact secrets of the run before any clipping, including across chunk boundaries and split UTF-8 characters. One limit stands: only exact text in the three encodings is replaced. A tool that prints a secret in another form, such as a JSON-escaped `\\/` in the base64 form or a URL-encoded form, still passes it through. The session secret is base64url, so this applies only to the operator key's base64 form.\n- P1 grants publishing to one appointed member under a separate grant. A wrong scope, pin, genesis, appointment, repository, journal gap or chain stops the cycle and reports nothing. The publisher never signs a kept report again. It reads no credential, and it pushes only to a local bare repository from the expected base. Any member who can `donate` chooses the page content, and the publisher writes that text into the repository as it is. That is the design of the shelf. The path rules confine the writes to `shelf/*.md`.\n\nSimplification: no required change. GS-4 replaces four separate pre-gate rules in `docs/testing.md` with one command.\n\nQualifications that stand: the GS-4 stale-identifier control is a scratch gate run that stopped at release reproduction. The P1 restart witness scripts its `unsent` ending, so it proves neither absence nor a Native refusal. P1 control attempt 1 was inconclusive before its tests ran. The P1 and LS-4 controls kept no raw child output under their normal helpers. P1 uses scripted membership and read authority, and its remote handoff uses the owner's Git. No hosted, provider, remote Git credential, release or deployment result follows. The cause of the Linux smoke failure is still open. This approval authorizes no push, landing, signing or deployment. The planner decides the landing, after CE-2 and LS-3.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e9c95baedd01ded6cf871557334c7a560ff86443","binding":"assigned","head":"5784e23d8197d5cbea819849af3830131449c874","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9a58331689d017641d6fecb896893e19b9ab93c5\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f7f7040b859b7912bc41bc1497e72b049e1a3dbc\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3acac8122156f2c7cfb2783767f48104a9c1bc34\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:76c1102dbb2031c323c163521ff7e6d493db01e6\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9a58331689d017641d6fecb896893e19b9ab93c5","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}